Sval: a tab moved to another window keeps its session state

tabbrowser's _swapBrowserDocShells swapped the browsers' permanentKey
properties after swapping their docshells. The swap sets each browsing
context's embedder, and CanonicalBrowsingContext::MaybeSetPermanentKey gives
the context the key its new element holds at that moment: the other tab's.
SessionStore files every update by the context's key, so whatever a moved
tab reported afterwards (form data, scroll, history) went under a key no tab
holds. SessionStore's onMoveToNewWindow copied the state across once, after
a flush, and threw when the update it needed had not been processed yet
(Mozilla bug 1938594, open, no fix upstream).

Swapping the keys first makes each context's key its element's. The moved
tab's state stays under its own key, so the copy, and its race, go.

